auth {
  mode: oauth2
}

auth:oauth2 {
  grant_type: authorization_code
  callback_url: {{IDP_REDIRECT_URI}}
  authorization_url: {{IDP_AUTHZ_EP}}
  access_token_url: {{IDP_TOKEN_EP}}
  refresh_token_url: {{IDP_TOKEN_EP}}
  client_id: {{IDP_CLIENT_ID}}
  client_secret: 
  scope: {{IDP_SCOPE}}
  state: {{STATE}}
  pkce: true
  credentials_placement: body
  credentials_id: credentials
  token_placement: header
  token_header_prefix: Bearer
  auto_fetch_token: true
  auto_refresh_token: true
}

docs {
  The rider-facing requests inherit this OAuth flow.

  PKCE is on and there is no client secret, because detour-app is a public
  client — a native app cannot keep one. The password grant is deliberately
  disabled on the realm, so this is the only way in; Bruno will open a browser
  the first time a request needs a token.

  Two credentials do not use it:

  - Dashboard requests carry a read-only API key in X-Api-Key. Issue one with
    ApiKeys > Issue a read-only dashboard key and paste it into API_KEY.
  - Health needs nothing at all.

  Admin requests inherit the same rider flow; the realm role decides whether
  they are answered. Sign in as a rider holding detour-admin.
}
